//RS /// c109 Phase 19: a GENERIC struct application `Pair<T>` / `Stack<Int>` (a `Type::Apply`)
//RS /// usable as a param/return/local value type. The base name must be a covered user struct
//RS /// (`struct_is_covered` — which admits type-var fields, Phase 19), and every type argument
//RS /// must itself be a covered value type OR a bare type variable. Imported struct shapes use
//RS /// their canonical qualified names in the same tables, so `owner::Stack<Int>` follows the
//RS /// identical TIR path. The Rust head is `__jet_<Name>::<args>` (the turbofish from
//RS /// `user_type_apply_rust`), resolved at lowering. `cx.rust_type` already renders
//RS /// `Type::Apply` to that head, so param/return/local typing is byte-identical to the AST
//RS /// path. (A non-generic `Type::Apply` would be malformed; sema only produces `Apply` for a
//RS /// generic struct/enum instantiation.)
