//RS /// c109 Phase 23: a DISTINCT type (`UserId :: distinct Int`, D-DIST1) usable as a
//RS /// param/return/local *value* type. A distinct type renders via `cx.rust_type` to its
//RS /// newtype `__jet_<Name>` (the `Type::Named` fallthrough in Context.rs), and the emitted
//RS /// `#[repr(transparent)]` newtype is `Copy` iff its base is (sema/codegen derive set) —
//RS /// but the param convention (`Read`→deref for a non-scalar Named) is decided exactly as
//RS /// for a struct, so passing/binding/returning one is byte-identical to the AST path with
//RS /// no new emit. Construction is the `is_distinct_ctor` `Call` shape; `.raw()` is the
//RS /// dedicated DistinctRaw method shape; `+`/`==` on a `#Numeric` distinct emit the native
//RS /// operator (`ast_operand_is_integer` returns `None` for a distinct-typed operand, so the
//RS /// overflow trap is never claimed — matching the AST path's plain `+`).
//RS pub(crate) fn is_covered_distinct_ty(ty: &Type, cx: &Cx) -> bool {
//RS     matches!(ty, Type::Named(name) if cx.is_distinct_type_name(name))
//RS }
//RS 
//RS /// c109 Phase 23: a named-tuple type `(x: Int, y: Int)` (S73/D-SG7, `Type::Tuple`)
//RS /// usable as a param/return/local value type. A tuple renders via `cx.rust_type` to a
//RS /// generated `#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq[, …])]` struct `JetTup_<hash>` (with
//RS /// `__jet_<field>` fields) emitted by `Tuples.rs` for every tuple SHAPE the program uses
//RS /// — so passing/binding/returning one is byte-identical to the AST path with no new
//RS /// emit. A tuple field read is the generic `Field` shape (`(t).__jet_<f>`); construction
//RS /// is the `TupleLit` shape; destructuring is the `BindPattern::Tuple` `let` form;
